                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "An OK match 3 spoiled by amateurish 2d art, an annoying tendency to crash and (worst of all) an annoying control scheme that makes manipulating the tiles hit and miss.\n\nOh it also has an annoying main menu,  you have to hit space rather than mouse to skip cutscenes, there's no way to set resolution, no graphics options.\n\nI thought the way to exit and save your progress would be to press b to retreat on the cutscene screen. Turns out this abandons your progress and the way to save it is to press escape mid game then delete. Good going devs. Thanks a bunch. Never mind, I don't really want to play this again anyway.\n\nAvoid. There are countless better match 3 games out there.",
